    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for the Austin Waves today is anchored by the middle-of-the-order firepower provided by **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**. **Kyle Tucker** is our premier play of the day with an 85.72 efficiency score; facing Tomoyuki Sugano in a hitter-friendly environment provides an elite environment for both power and run production. **Andy Pages** follows closely behind at 75.63, benefiting from the same favorable matchup against Sugano\u2019s projected 4.93 xERA. While **Drake Baldwin** rounds out our top trio at 72.03, his utility as a leadoff hitter against the vulnerable Bailey Ober makes him a high-floor selection, provided the lineup confirmation aligns with our projections.\n\nStrategic platoon and park adjustments played a significant role in today\u2019s optimization. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tough lefty in Shane McClanahan\u2014driving his score down to 53.52\u2014we are forced to ride out the matchup due to his overall ceiling. Conversely, **Dominic Smith** receives a meaningful boost to 58.63 because of his platoon advantage against Ober, nearly crossing the threshold into the \"Strong\" category. The most difficult bench decision involved weighing **Jackson Merrill** against our depth; his 53.85 score keeps him in the lineup primarily due to a positive dynamic platoon adjustment against Nolan McLean, even though the opposing SP skill slightly dampens his raw output. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all players, as any downward shift in batting order for **Drake Baldwin** or **Sam Antonacci**\u2014who is already skating on thin ice with a 45.05 score due to a difficult L/L matchup against Shota Imanaga\u2014could necessitate a roster pivot. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL, our depth is thin, and we have no room for error; the bench remains stagnant as **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Nasim Nunez** are currently unavailable due to team off-days. We will continue to monitor the status of **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara** should weather or late scratches force a mid-day rotation adjustment.",
